[Unit]
Description=Reboot system daily at midnight

[Timer]
# Every day at midnight
OnCalendar=*-*-* 00:00:00
# Keep Persistent=true so it runs on boot if missed
# But the script itself will be smart about when to actually reboot
Persistent=true

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target


## How This Works:

### Scenario 1: PC Running at Midnight ✅

#00:00 - Timer triggers
#00:00 - Script checks: hour = 00 (nighttime)
#00:00 - REBOOTS immediately


### Scenario 2: PC Off at Midnight, Boots at 8 AM ✅

#Friday 00:00 - Timer should have run (PC was off)
#Monday 08:00 - PC boots
#Monday 08:01 - Timer runs because Persistent=true
#Monday 08:01 - Script checks: hour = 08 (daytime)
#Monday 08:01 - Schedules reboot for midnight instead
#Monday 08:01 - User can work normally
#Tuesday 00:00 - PC reboots as scheduled


### Scenario 3: PC Off Over Weekend, Boots Monday 8 AM ✅

#Fri 00:00 - Missed
#Sat 00:00 - Missed
#Sun 00:00 - Missed
#Mon 08:00 - PC boots
#Mon 08:01 - Timer runs (one catch-up run)
#Mon 08:01 - Script: hour = 08 (daytime)
#Mon 08:01 - Schedules reboot for midnight
#Mon 08:01 - User works normally
#Tue 00:00 - Reboots


### Scenario 4: User Working Late at 11:30 PM ✅

#23:30 - User still logged in
#00:00 - Timer triggers
#00:00 - Script checks: hour = 00 (nighttime)
#00:00 - REBOOTS (tough luck, save your work!)
